/ bugs: the fixes item-doors' audit, the goal channel's race and packages' Windows window left, plus Ingi's three
/ yeses from fast-apps. This goal is the plan's index and its proof: each stage is a goal, each comment a behaviour we
/ want, and the step under it runs the test that proves it. The plang here is intent: each test is written so it goes
/ red before its stage, and the coder makes it green. The text is start.md.
Start
- call Stage1
- call Stage2
- call Stage3
- call Stage4
- call Stage5
- call Stage6
- call Stage7

Stage1
/ an llm test asks OpenAI nothing when its answers are in its file: a run with no key passes — plang test
/ /module/llm (each of the six, no OPENAI_API_KEY)
/ a question not in the file is asked once and added to it; the second run asks nothing — C# test
/ LlmAnswersFileTests (ANewQuestion_IsAskedOnce_ThenRead)
/ a changed prompt is a new question: the old answer is never served for it — C# test LlmAnswersFileTests
/ (AChangedPrompt_IsNotServedTheOldAnswer)
/ the key never lands in the file: it holds the request body and the endpoint path, never a header — C# test
/ LlmAnswersFileTests (TheKey_NeverLandsInTheFile)
/ test.setting.llm=live asks OpenAI and writes nothing — C# test LlmAnswersFileTests (Live_WritesNothing)
/ the cache's own test still proves the cache: a first ask misses, a second hits
- call /module/llm/LlmCache

Stage2
/ export refuses: exporting a private key waits for critical actions — C# test IdentityExportTests
/ (Export_Refuses_UntilCriticalActions, TheExportQuestion_IsNeverAsked)
/ a failed "always" save answers its error, not Ok — C# test GrantKeepTests (AFailedAlwaysSave_AnswersItsError)
/ a one-time yes on the os folder keeps its standing grant: read and execute stay — C# test GrantKeepTests
/ (AOneTimeYes_KeepsTheStandingGrant)
/ a persisted grant can't open the stores' folder, with the grant really saved — C# test
/ PersistedGrantCannotOverrideStoresTests (Find is non-null after the persist)
/ a bug inside an ask surfaces as itself, not as a "no"; a cancelled input is a "no" — C# test ConsentAskTests
/ (ABugInTheAsk_IsNotADenial, ACancelledInput_IsADenial)

Stage3
/ a json number slot holding true is refused, naming the slot — C# test JsonReaderTests (ANumberSlot_RefusesABool)
/ a bad size, parallel or choice from a peer lands as its own error, never a 500 — C# test TypeReaderErrorTests
/ (one case per reader)

Stage4
/ each write to a goal channel sees its own message, 20 writes at once
- call /channel/goal/EachWriteSeesItsOwnMessage
/ each iteration of a parallel foreach that writes to a goal channel sees its own message
- call /channel/goal/ParallelWritesSeeTheirOwn

Stage5
/ each command line plang can't read is refused, naming the argument — C# test StartRefusalTests (a second
/ positional, a dotted positional, --test=module/x, --debug=false with a debug setting, a repeat differing in case)
/ %path% is the landed root, not the folder as typed — C# test ExecutorTests (APathIsSeededFromTheRoot)

Stage6
/ a path beside the root that starts with its name is not in it (/root2 is not under /root) — C# test
/ ValidatePathTests (ASiblingWithTheRootsPrefix_IsNotUnderIt)
/ OsTrustTests passes on Windows: no / separator in its compare — the Windows run
/ the window applies frames through Shown and decodes QOI through Qoi; a frame larger than screen.setting.max is
/ BadFrame before any decode, whatever its message says — C# test WindowFrameTests (Linux, through the shared code)
/ a patch before the first frame decodes nothing and breaks nothing — C# test WindowFrameTests
/ (APatchBeforeTheFirstFrame)

Stage7
/ module.remove answers data: true removed, false not there, ModuleShared refused — C# test ModuleRemoveTests
/ an app is born with the console's channels or without, by a choice that names both — C# test AppConsoleTests
/ a channel is born in its list: its list and actor are set at birth, never after — C# test ChannelBirthTests
